cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "research-ml-modeling: a reviewer-grade machine-learning pipeline for spectroscopic and tabular predictive modelling"
abstract: >-
  A command-line pipeline and agent skill that turns raw tabular or spectroscopic data into a
  publication-ready modelling report: data audit, nested grouped repeated cross-validation,
  Y-randomization permutation tests, four applicability-domain methods with validity testing,
  cluster-bootstrap confidence intervals, publication-quality figures, a draft Methods paragraph
  and a reviewer-response checklist. Every reported number is recomputable from the pooled
  out-of-fold predictions, and provenance is pinned by three hashes.
type: software
